# PrivaPilot reasoning gateway configuration.
# Copy to `.env` (same directory) — `npm run dev:server` loads it automatically.
# Every value is optional: with none set, the gateway auto-probes Ollama and
# LM Studio on the loopback and otherwise uses the deterministic offline reasoner.

# --- Gateway ---
# PORT=4501

# --- Option A: local Ollama (default, nothing to configure) ---
# Only set this if Ollama listens somewhere other than 127.0.0.1:11434.
# OLLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1:11434
# Pin a specific pulled model. If it is not installed, the gateway logs a warning
# and falls back to an installed one rather than failing every request.
# VLM_MODEL=qwen2.5vl

# --- Option B: local LM Studio ---
# LM_STUDIO_HOST=127.0.0.1:1234

# --- Option C: any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (OpenRouter, Groq, Together, ...) ---
# THIS IS WHAT THE PROJECT CURRENTLY USES. Must be the full chat-completions URL,
# not just the host. Copy these three lines into .env and add your own key.
#
# Qwen2.5-VL is Apache-2.0 open weights and runs locally via `ollama pull qwen2.5vl`,
# so the hosted endpoint is a deployment choice rather than a dependency - which is
# exactly what SIH26171 permits: "any offline deployable (open-source/open-weights)
# model ... During SIH they can use cloud hosted version of these."
# VLM_ENDPOINT=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions
# VLM_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
# VLM_MODEL=qwen/qwen2.5-vl-72b-instruct

# --- Timeouts (milliseconds) ---
# How long a single inference may take. Local vision models on CPU are slow.
# VLM_TIMEOUT_MS=90000
# How long a backend availability probe may take.
# VLM_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS=4000

# --- Local Ollama context window ---
# Ollama's default context (2048-4096) silently TRUNCATES the prompt once a
# screenshot is attached - a 1280x800 capture becomes thousands of vision tokens.
# The model then reasons over a partial element list and returns invalid JSON,
# which looks like a bad model but is a misconfiguration. Raise if you see the
# offline reasoner kicking in on a local model that should be working.
# VLM_NUM_CTX=8192
